# .monitor.env — credentials + tuning for scripts/oracle-staleness-check.sh
#
# The script reads this file from a fixed path on the homelab:
#   /home/muhaven/Project/Fhenix/MuHaven/.monitor.env
#
# Override the path at runtime via the MONITOR_ENV_FILE env var (for
# testing locally without touching the repo root).
#
# Usage on the homelab (one-time setup, see development/DEV_WAVE_3/
# HOMELAB_DEPLOY.md "Oracle staleness monitor" section for the full
# walkthrough including crontab installation):
#
#   ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_muhaven_vm muhaven@192.168.1.52
#   cp scripts/.monitor.env.example /home/muhaven/Project/Fhenix/MuHaven/.monitor.env
#   # edit and fill the <<FILL_*>> placeholders
#   chmod 600 /home/muhaven/Project/Fhenix/MuHaven/.monitor.env
#
# The script degrades gracefully — when this file is absent OR the
# TELEGRAM_* vars are unset, it still runs and prints alerts to stdout
# (captured by the crontab redirect to /var/log/muhaven-oracle-monitor.log).
# Telegram delivery is only the loud-channel addition.

# ── Telegram alert routing ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Re-use the existing operator bot. Token + chat ID are stored in
# /home/muhaven/Project/Fhenix/MuHaven/telegram-bot/.env (or backend/.env)
# already; copy the same values here. Keep this file at 0600 — it
# carries the same secret weight as the source env files.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=<<FILL_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN>>

# To find your numeric chat ID, message @userinfobot on Telegram, OR
# read it from `docker compose logs -f telegram-bot` after sending the
# bot a `/start` from your Telegram client.
TELEGRAM_OPERATOR_CHAT_ID=<<FILL_TELEGRAM_OPERATOR_CHAT_ID>>

# ── Optional overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Staleness threshold in hours. Contract's max-staleness is 36h.
# nav-publisher refreshes a token only when its age crosses ½ of
# max-staleness (= 18h for a 36h window — see
# nav-publisher/src/publisher.ts:232), so under normal operation a token
# oscillates between 0 and ~27h before being refreshed. Default 28h
# stays above that band so we only alert on REAL stalls, while leaving
# 8h hard-slack before contract reverts. Lower to 18h if you want a
# louder canary for "publisher might be slipping a cycle"; lower to 12h
# only if you've also lowered the publisher's half-window to a quarter.
# THRESHOLD_HR=28

# Arbitrum Sepolia RPC endpoint. Default uses the public Arb Sepolia
# rollup RPC; set this to a private RPC (Alchemy, etc.) if you start
# hitting rate limits on the cron schedule.
# ARB_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://sepolia-rollup.arbitrum.io/rpc

# TokenRegistry proxy on Arb Sepolia. Default matches
# deployments/arb-sepolia-v2.json — override only if rotating to a new
# registry (rare; would be a v3 deploy event).
# TOKEN_REGISTRY_ADDR=0x4915E9Aa034244e299fb1609792D66b9fFAbf885

# Hard override of the token roster — comma-separated `address:symbol`
# pairs. Bypasses TokenRegistry enumeration entirely. Useful for:
#   - testing the alert path against a sentinel-stale token
#   - excluding a specific token while the rest of the roster runs
# MUHAVEN_NAV_TOKEN_ROSTER=0x8D77cCf0a3a56c976a7DEAe59aF1D27f27407b0D:TBILL1 0x93e813e924A96441181A01171Cd1E20FaaC87AcF:GOLD1
